{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LobachevskyDerivativeAnalytic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.LobachevskyDerivativeAnalytic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.analyticOnNhd_neg_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.analyticOnNhd_neg_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyDerivativeAnalytic.lean#L86-L90","doc":"**`Λ'` is real-analytic on the whole open interval `(0, π)`** (the\n`AnalyticOnNhd` form the identity theorem consumes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.analyticAt_neg_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.analyticAt_neg_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyDerivativeAnalytic.lean#L70-L84","doc":"**`Λ'(t) = −log(2 sin t)` is real-analytic on `(0, π)`.**  On `(0, π)`,\n`sin t > 0`, so `2 sin t > 0` and `Real.log` is analytic there\n(`AnalyticAt.log`); precompose with the analytic `Real.sin` and negate.\n\nThis is the analytic input the obtuse ideal-tetrahedron volume identity's\nanalytic-continuation route consumes for its derivative; it does not by itself\nmake `Λ` analytic (see the file header). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.analyticAt_real_cos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.analyticAt_real_cos","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyDerivativeAnalytic.lean#L64-L68","doc":"**`Real.cos` is real-analytic at every point.**  Same route through the\nentire complex `cos`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.analyticAt_real_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.analyticAt_real_sin","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/LobachevskyDerivativeAnalytic.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**`Real.sin` is real-analytic at every point.**  The complex `sin` is\nentire (`Complex.analyticAt_sin`); its restriction to the reals along\n`ofReal`, read off by the real part, is `Real.sin` (`Complex.sin_ofReal_re`).\nMathlib proves the ℂ side but names no ℝ-side lemma, so this fills the gap. ","signatureChunk":0}]}